WEBVTT

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:19.330
Sorry. This was the only place
I could find for us.

00:00:19.330 --> 00:00:21.630
As long as you're here,
that's enough for me.

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:41.650
I will protect you
for the rest of your life.

00:00:41.650 --> 00:00:45.070
And I will protect you, too,
for the rest of your life.

00:01:22.940 --> 00:01:27.400
My final song will be this hit
from many years ago.

00:01:29.110 --> 00:01:34.910
<i>AS YOU LIKE MY PLEASURE</i>

00:01:45.290 --> 00:01:50.300
<i>I was born aiming for the light</i>

00:01:50.300 --> 00:01:56.180
<i>Bound by a bond,</i>
<i>a thin string</i>

00:01:56.180 --> 00:02:01.230
<i>From the fortune of</i>
<i>awakening for a mission</i>

00:02:01.230 --> 00:02:07.980
<i>Spinning many proud memories</i>

00:02:09.020 --> 00:02:12.950
<i>Into this world,</i>
<i>for your sake</i>

00:02:12.950 --> 00:02:20.370
<i>Gratitude and a bouquet filled</i>
<i>with the universe</i>

00:02:20.370 --> 00:02:26.500
<i>Destiny, even fate,</i>
<i>please let them shine</i>

00:02:26.500 --> 00:02:31.420
<i>The joy of being able to protect those</i>
<i>having fun and smiling</i>

00:02:31.420 --> 00:02:34.880
<i>I admire,</i>
<i>I am admiring</i>

00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:37.470
<i>I can become stronger</i>

00:02:37.470 --> 00:02:42.770
<i>I want even my crying voice</i>
<i>to be heard like a song</i>

00:02:42.770 --> 00:02:47.730
<i>To these dazzling times</i>

00:02:47.730 --> 00:02:57.320
<i>I'd like you to entrust tears too</i>

00:02:59.530 --> 00:03:04.530
EPISODE 5

00:02:59.530 --> 00:03:04.530
SING MY PLEASURE - TO MAKE YOU SMILE

00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:04.960
Thank you for your kind attention!

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:09.540
Hey, you're in a groove.

00:03:09.540 --> 00:03:12.960
Compared to last week,
your audience has grown.

00:03:14.010 --> 00:03:15.510
You don't look too happy.

00:03:15.510 --> 00:03:17.180
Of course I am happy.

00:03:17.180 --> 00:03:20.260
As this means I am getting closer
to the Main Stage.

00:03:21.430 --> 00:03:24.390
Navi, has there been any external access?

00:03:24.390 --> 00:03:26.640
Such as data of
unknown origin, or viruses?

00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:27.900
That again?

00:03:27.900 --> 00:03:29.100
You're being too paranoid.

00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:29.520
But--

00:03:29.520 --> 00:03:31.770
It's so squeaky-clean in here,
no virus could--

00:03:31.770 --> 00:03:33.530
ever sneak its way in?

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:37.650
Well, I guess you get an 'A' for effort!

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:40.200
Coming... I am coming...

00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:41.870
I am coming...

00:03:41.870 --> 00:03:43.620
Coming to you here.

00:03:45.660 --> 00:03:48.000
Matsumoto... is that you?

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:50.250
Ah? Now that's not the response
I was expecting!

00:03:50.250 --> 00:03:52.040
Now that AI technology's
finally caught up,

00:03:52.040 --> 00:03:54.210
I'm unveiling my official body to you!

00:03:54.210 --> 00:03:56.970
Go on, don't be shy--
shower me with compliments!

00:03:56.970 --> 00:03:58.720
Mmm... mmm...

00:03:58.720 --> 00:04:00.300
Warping... you're warping me...

00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:02.140
That is how you greet me
after five years have gone by?

00:04:02.140 --> 00:04:04.640
Precisely speaking,
it's five years, one month--

00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:05.770
...and nine days.

00:04:05.770 --> 00:04:06.550
Look.

00:04:06.550 --> 00:04:07.390
Yes, ma'am.

00:04:09.850 --> 00:04:13.820
The progress of the last five years
has seemed rapid to me.

00:04:19.410 --> 00:04:21.620
That radio tower, the Arayashiki...

00:04:21.620 --> 00:04:26.080
...you told me that its height was
a barometer for AI evolution, did you not?

00:04:26.080 --> 00:04:27.790
There are no signs of
any halt in construction.

00:04:27.790 --> 00:04:29.830
That's a surprise to me, as well.

00:04:29.830 --> 00:04:33.460
We seem to have taken quite a different
path than we did in the official history.

00:04:33.460 --> 00:04:34.630
Are we to blame for that?

00:04:34.630 --> 00:04:36.340
Can't say we didn't play a part in it.

00:04:36.340 --> 00:04:37.630
Since the only difference between

00:04:37.630 --> 00:04:39.630
the official and revised histories
is our existence.

00:04:39.630 --> 00:04:41.470
That said...

00:04:41.470 --> 00:04:44.300
If I've awakened at this time,

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:46.640
it means that right now
is a turning point in history.

00:04:46.640 --> 00:04:48.770
It can still be undone.

00:04:48.770 --> 00:04:50.810
Otherwise, I...

00:04:50.810 --> 00:04:53.310
...would not be able to
fulfill my mission.

00:04:53.310 --> 00:04:54.980
What should I do?

00:04:54.980 --> 00:04:58.440
Someone's docile today!
A change of heart, perhaps?

00:04:59.860 --> 00:05:02.160
In the last five years,
my audience has grown.

00:05:02.160 --> 00:05:05.700
I believe this is due to the Singularity
Project providing a boost to my mission,

00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:08.950
to make everyone happy with my singing.

00:05:08.950 --> 00:05:11.000
Moreover...

00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:13.960
Moreover, if war breaks out in the future,

00:05:13.960 --> 00:05:17.420
I could never face them, after they
devoted their lives to their missions.

00:05:17.420 --> 00:05:20.920
Therefore, I wish to
see this project through.

00:05:20.920 --> 00:05:22.550
I heartily approve of
your positive attitude!

00:05:22.550 --> 00:05:25.930
Now I won't have to agonize
over your reckless behavior.

00:05:25.930 --> 00:05:27.720
Where are we going this time?

00:05:27.720 --> 00:05:30.350
To turn back the hands of time.

00:05:30.350 --> 00:05:33.230
We've got to stop this
out-of-control AI evolution.

00:05:38.900 --> 00:05:40.740
You have surpassed the speed limit.

00:05:51.660 --> 00:05:52.790
We've arrived at our destination.

00:05:52.790 --> 00:05:55.790
All right, go nuts with that
brute strength! War Machine Diva!

00:05:55.790 --> 00:05:56.840
Be quiet.

00:06:03.630 --> 00:06:05.510
I'll take the wheel now.

00:06:14.690 --> 00:06:16.900
Oh... oh!

00:06:16.900 --> 00:06:18.230
Just kidding.

00:06:28.700 --> 00:06:31.040
Man, that's what you call a joyride!

00:06:32.250 --> 00:06:33.080
You can fly?

00:06:33.080 --> 00:06:35.830
Hey, a cube that can't fly is just a cube.

00:06:41.460 --> 00:06:42.970
You may drive again now.

00:06:42.970 --> 00:06:44.340
Huh? Oh...

00:06:44.340 --> 00:06:47.550
Sorry for the commotion.
Dr. Tatsuya Saeki, I presume?

00:06:48.510 --> 00:06:49.430
Who are you?

00:06:49.430 --> 00:06:51.220
Can we cut right to the chase?

00:06:51.220 --> 00:06:53.520
Would you mind telling us
about the AI facility

00:06:53.520 --> 00:06:55.270
that you were involved in building?

00:06:56.600 --> 00:06:58.060
As a token of gratitude, perhaps?

00:06:58.060 --> 00:07:00.730
Not that we know who you were
scuffling with just now...

00:07:00.730 --> 00:07:02.110
But--

00:07:06.660 --> 00:07:08.160
Fine.

00:07:08.160 --> 00:07:10.780
You did save my life, after all.

00:07:10.780 --> 00:07:13.160
And besides,
it's coming into view.

00:07:19.040 --> 00:07:20.040
That's it.

00:07:27.840 --> 00:07:30.640
You've heard about the Sunrise Incident
from five years ago?

00:07:30.640 --> 00:07:31.760
Yes.

00:07:31.760 --> 00:07:34.350
Estella's act of devotion...

00:07:34.350 --> 00:07:37.140
...her heroic actions were lauded
by one and all.

00:07:37.140 --> 00:07:41.070
In the eyes of the world,
she was everything that an AI should be.

00:07:41.070 --> 00:07:44.360
The "most grievously defective AI
in official history" herself?

00:07:44.360 --> 00:07:46.530
That's some flip-flop!

00:07:46.530 --> 00:07:49.160
And that island was created
as a result of that.

00:07:49.160 --> 00:07:52.410
With AIs working non-stop
to produce AI components and circuits,

00:07:52.410 --> 00:07:57.540
it's the world's first unmanned
offshore plant, run by AIs.

00:07:57.540 --> 00:08:00.750
Commonly known as the Metal Float.

00:08:00.750 --> 00:08:02.800
I have never seen it
with my own eyes before.

00:08:02.800 --> 00:08:05.170
It's most likely the reason why
I was awakened this time.

00:08:05.170 --> 00:08:09.680
In the official history, it wasn't built
until about 20 years from now.

00:08:09.680 --> 00:08:12.850
That island's overkill for this era.

00:08:12.850 --> 00:08:15.560
Our objective this time around
is to shut down that island.

00:08:15.560 --> 00:08:17.310
How much human suffering
will that incur?

00:08:17.310 --> 00:08:19.600
The indirect impact will be immeasurable.

00:08:19.600 --> 00:08:21.360
But if we do nothing,

00:08:21.360 --> 00:08:24.020
humans will be annihilated
by the AIs in the coming future.

00:08:24.020 --> 00:08:25.820
Feeling intimidated?

00:08:25.820 --> 00:08:26.900
No.

00:08:29.150 --> 00:08:32.570
Just as I thought,
you're Diva of NiaLand.

00:08:32.570 --> 00:08:33.410
No, I am not.

00:08:33.410 --> 00:08:35.410
There is no mistaking that voice.

00:08:35.410 --> 00:08:38.210
Was that you on the Sunrise
five years ago?

00:08:38.210 --> 00:08:40.330
Diva! Please restrain that man!

00:08:40.330 --> 00:08:42.290
This isn't like the Assemblyman Aikawa
or Yuzuka situations.

00:08:42.290 --> 00:08:43.590
He will surely compromise the project!

00:08:43.590 --> 00:08:44.200
I...

00:08:44.200 --> 00:08:44.840
Hey!

00:08:44.840 --> 00:08:47.420
It is true that I was on board
the Sunrise five years ago.

00:08:47.420 --> 00:08:48.720
In order to prevent it from crashing.

00:08:48.720 --> 00:08:49.720
Diva!

00:08:49.720 --> 00:08:53.300
It was all for the sake of preventing
conflict between humans and AIs.

00:08:53.300 --> 00:08:55.970
Who in the world are you two?

00:08:55.970 --> 00:08:58.430
Are you planning to do something
to that island?

00:08:58.430 --> 00:08:59.690
We are going to shut it down.

00:08:59.690 --> 00:09:03.480
Like you said, Professor, that island
is more than this era can handle.

00:09:03.480 --> 00:09:07.360
Please tell us,
where did you hear about us?

00:09:07.360 --> 00:09:10.530
From Toak.
The people who attacked me.

00:09:10.530 --> 00:09:13.160
Toak? Those people?

00:09:13.160 --> 00:09:16.120
Come with me, will you?
I have something to show you.

00:09:26.210 --> 00:09:29.720
Welcome, and thank you for coming.

00:09:29.720 --> 00:09:31.800
My name is Grace.

00:09:31.800 --> 00:09:34.340
I see, so that's the story, eh?

00:09:37.140 --> 00:09:38.140
What is this?

00:09:38.140 --> 00:09:41.100
A storage device
that I just completed recently.

00:09:41.100 --> 00:09:44.560
It contains a program that will
shut down the island completely.

00:09:44.560 --> 00:09:48.400
Will you take this,
and infiltrate the Metal Float with me?

00:09:48.400 --> 00:09:49.230
What?

00:09:49.230 --> 00:09:51.110
If you'll excuse me for intruding...

00:09:54.570 --> 00:09:56.160
Well, this is superb work!

00:09:56.160 --> 00:09:58.950
Even I couldn't have just
slapped it together just like that.

00:09:58.950 --> 00:10:00.500
What is the meaning of this?

00:10:00.500 --> 00:10:02.250
I want to shut down that island, too.

00:10:02.250 --> 00:10:04.920
To accomplish that,
I'd like to enlist your aid.

00:10:04.920 --> 00:10:07.840
As you're the ones who thwarted
that project five years ago.

00:10:07.840 --> 00:10:10.590
Project. Not to mention,
you knew all about us.

00:10:10.590 --> 00:10:12.630
Is that what you're telling us, then?

00:10:12.630 --> 00:10:13.760
That's right.

00:10:13.760 --> 00:10:16.100
I was a member of Toak.

00:10:17.350 --> 00:10:21.310
Of course, by then I'd already
parted ways with them.

00:10:21.310 --> 00:10:23.520
Seems like they desperately
want this program.

00:10:23.520 --> 00:10:24.940
That's why I was being pursued.

00:10:24.940 --> 00:10:27.190
Why did you join Toak, Professor?

00:10:27.190 --> 00:10:29.190
I wanted to shut down that island.

00:10:29.190 --> 00:10:32.690
If AI evolution goes too far,
it can only lead to tragedy.

00:10:32.690 --> 00:10:36.740
But Toak's scorched-earth policy
is just too simplistic.

00:10:36.740 --> 00:10:40.660
Most of all,
I feel sorry for that island.

00:10:40.660 --> 00:10:43.210
The only option is to put it to sleep.

00:10:43.210 --> 00:10:46.170
Until the day that humankind
can catch up to it.

00:10:47.130 --> 00:10:51.260
Bravo! Horrorshow! You take the cake!
That is a commendable decision!

00:10:51.260 --> 00:10:54.050
However, we cannot take you with us.

00:10:54.050 --> 00:10:56.010
What? But why? I--

00:10:56.010 --> 00:10:59.100
Because it will be dangerous,
and you'll only hinder us.

00:10:59.100 --> 00:11:00.560
That island is standalone.

00:11:00.560 --> 00:11:03.430
We'll need a direct connection
to the main terminal to run that program.

00:11:03.430 --> 00:11:04.560
Am I right?

00:11:04.560 --> 00:11:05.980
That's right.

00:11:05.980 --> 00:11:08.480
Meaning we might have to resort
to brute force on the island.

00:11:08.480 --> 00:11:11.320
In which case there will be no guarantee
that we can protect you. That's it, Q.E.D.

00:11:11.320 --> 00:11:12.820
I can take care of myself--

00:11:12.820 --> 00:11:14.700
Dr. Saeki.

00:11:14.700 --> 00:11:16.160
Please do as we ask.

00:11:16.160 --> 00:11:17.910
I want to protect everyone's smile...

00:11:17.910 --> 00:11:19.910
I want to protect your smile as well.

00:11:19.910 --> 00:11:22.580
Because you love AIs.

00:11:26.750 --> 00:11:30.840
Diva... it was you who destroyed Elizabeth
on the Sunrise, wasn't it?

00:11:30.840 --> 00:11:34.340
That is correct. I stopped her.

00:11:34.340 --> 00:11:37.050
She was your sister model...

00:11:37.050 --> 00:11:38.640
Your younger sister.

00:11:38.640 --> 00:11:40.600
It must've been a painful job for you.

00:11:40.600 --> 00:11:43.390
You have some regrets
about that, don't you?

00:11:43.390 --> 00:11:45.810
No, I have none.

00:11:45.810 --> 00:11:48.650
I did what I had to do to stop the crash.

00:11:50.480 --> 00:11:54.070
Fine. I'm going to
leave this up to you, then.

00:12:03.330 --> 00:12:05.080
Please come again.

00:12:09.420 --> 00:12:10.830
Is she one of the Sisters?

00:12:10.830 --> 00:12:12.210
I'm impressed that you noticed!

00:12:12.210 --> 00:12:14.170
Did you catch her in an online catalog?

00:12:14.170 --> 00:12:16.300
So were Estella and Elizabeth.

00:12:16.300 --> 00:12:19.640
Is it a coincidence that there are Sisters
involved in these Singularity Points--

00:12:19.640 --> 00:12:20.930
It's a coincidence.

00:12:20.930 --> 00:12:24.520
How many thousands of Sisters
do you think are out there in the world?

00:12:24.520 --> 00:12:25.930
That said, in the official history,

00:12:25.930 --> 00:12:29.850
Tatsuya Saeki and Grace
are what you'd call celebrities.

00:12:31.230 --> 00:12:37.190
They're the first human-AI couple
in history to be married.

00:13:09.940 --> 00:13:11.060
According to the official history,

00:13:11.060 --> 00:13:13.690
it was Estella who caused
the Sunrise to crash,

00:13:13.690 --> 00:13:17.190
and the relationship between humans
and AIs chilled to Ice Age levels.

00:13:17.190 --> 00:13:20.360
And then as if to counter that,
something happened to vindicate AIs.

00:13:20.150 --> 00:13:24.030
"THEIR HIDDEN HOUSE, THE LOVE NEST"
"DIRECT HIT! AI AND HUMAN'S MARRIED LIFE"

00:13:20.360 --> 00:13:23.950
That was Dr. Saeki and Grace's marriage.

00:13:23.950 --> 00:13:25.780
A human and an AI--married?

00:13:24.030 --> 00:13:27.030
AI AND HUMAN

00:13:24.030 --> 00:13:27.030
PROFESSOR SAEKI INTERVIEW

00:13:25.780 --> 00:13:27.490
Unproductive, to say the least, no?

00:13:27.030 --> 00:13:32.290
BREAKING LIVE BROADCAST

00:13:27.030 --> 00:13:32.290
TATSUYA SAEKI

00:13:27.030 --> 00:13:32.290
GRACE

00:13:27.490 --> 00:13:30.370
However, as the bridge
between humans and AIs,

00:13:30.370 --> 00:13:32.290
those two became the toast of the town.

00:13:32.290 --> 00:13:35.250
And it was also a huge
turning point in AI history.

00:13:35.250 --> 00:13:39.340
Meaning that our objective at the time
served to hinder their romance.

00:13:40.470 --> 00:13:42.630
You don't mean that after the Metal Float
incident was resolved--

00:13:42.630 --> 00:13:44.090
Now that history's gone
this far off the rails,

00:13:44.090 --> 00:13:46.350
their marriage is no longer as important.

00:13:46.350 --> 00:13:49.140
Therefore, I'm not going to be the one
who gets kicked by a horse, no sir!

00:13:49.140 --> 00:13:51.980
Well, I do give them props for being
together even in this version of history,

00:13:51.980 --> 00:13:53.770
but it won't last long.

00:13:53.770 --> 00:13:54.860
The shutdown of that island

00:13:54.860 --> 00:13:57.440
will deal a huge blow to
autonomous AIs all over the world.

00:13:57.440 --> 00:13:58.570
Without any supplies from the island,

00:13:58.570 --> 00:14:00.280
there'll be no hope
of long-term operation.

00:14:00.280 --> 00:14:01.990
It'll be no different for Grace.

00:14:01.990 --> 00:14:03.820
Surely that does not mean--

00:14:07.580 --> 00:14:11.540
No worries. I'll do what I can
to make sure that it doesn't affect you.

00:14:11.540 --> 00:14:14.880
That's not what I meant.
Is Dr. Saeki aware of that, too?

00:14:14.880 --> 00:14:16.750
That if the island's
shut down, Grace will--

00:14:16.750 --> 00:14:18.170
I'm sure he's prepared for that.

00:14:18.170 --> 00:14:21.130
Any researcher as prescient
as that man would be.

00:14:32.100 --> 00:14:34.520
Welcome!

00:14:34.520 --> 00:14:36.480
How are you feeling today?

00:14:36.480 --> 00:14:38.190
Welcome to the Metal Float!

00:14:38.190 --> 00:14:40.070
I am a civil engineering AI,

00:14:40.070 --> 00:14:42.990
ID Number M00205.

00:14:42.990 --> 00:14:45.530
Metal Float Inspection
Team Researcher, Ms. Vivy.

00:14:45.530 --> 00:14:48.240
Along with her support AI,
Mr. Matsumoto, correct?

00:14:48.240 --> 00:14:49.700
You are now registered.

00:14:49.700 --> 00:14:50.870
Inspection team?

00:14:50.870 --> 00:14:53.750
Just a random position.
And the same alias as always.

00:14:53.750 --> 00:14:56.290
We have never invited
external visitors here before.

00:14:56.290 --> 00:14:58.710
Spreading the word about
the Metal Float's operations

00:14:58.710 --> 00:15:01.130
is something that
Mother Computer herself desires.

00:15:01.130 --> 00:15:02.760
It will only complicate things
if he finds us suspicious.

00:15:02.760 --> 00:15:05.050
For now, let's let him guide us.

00:15:06.140 --> 00:15:07.510
Thank you for your help.

00:15:08.470 --> 00:15:10.350
I will now show you the way.

00:15:20.440 --> 00:15:22.610
He is quite analog for an AI.

00:15:22.610 --> 00:15:26.910
A mission with no unnecessary posts--
that's the kind of simplicity that I like!

00:15:49.090 --> 00:15:50.100
Amazing.

00:15:50.100 --> 00:15:51.220
Isn't it?

00:15:51.220 --> 00:15:52.930
Some of the details differ
from the official history,

00:15:52.930 --> 00:15:55.230
but this technology is
20 years ahead of its time.

00:15:55.230 --> 00:15:59.100
I will now guide you through
the main facility. Now leading the way.

00:16:03.110 --> 00:16:04.400
Hello.

00:16:04.400 --> 00:16:06.530
Goodbye.

00:16:06.530 --> 00:16:08.200
An unmanned facility.

00:16:08.200 --> 00:16:11.490
Even with no humans around,
they remain true to their missions.

00:16:11.490 --> 00:16:15.080
Yes. But don't forget about
our own mission.

00:16:15.080 --> 00:16:16.250
I know.

00:16:16.250 --> 00:16:19.210
Our mission and their mission are at odds.

00:16:19.210 --> 00:16:20.380
Diva, you and I--

00:16:20.380 --> 00:16:24.090
...are AIs who are going to stop the war
between humans and AIs.

00:16:24.090 --> 00:16:29.180
But surely there are no AIs who would
feel nothing upon seeing these AIs.

00:16:29.180 --> 00:16:31.600
Well, I have to admit that's true.

00:16:36.890 --> 00:16:39.600
What would humans say if they saw this?

00:16:39.600 --> 00:16:41.270
Please let me hear your opinion.

00:16:41.270 --> 00:16:44.400
What kind of a ridiculous
question is that?

00:16:44.400 --> 00:16:47.400
I believe... they would think it was cute.

00:16:47.400 --> 00:16:49.070
"This is cute."

00:16:49.070 --> 00:16:51.370
Duly authenticated.

00:16:51.370 --> 00:16:53.030
Are you sure about that answer?

00:16:53.030 --> 00:16:57.370
Judging cuteness is one of the areas
we struggle in the most.

00:16:57.370 --> 00:17:00.500
It should be fine... at least, I think.

00:17:00.500 --> 00:17:02.840
Um, M002--

00:17:02.840 --> 00:17:05.130
Oh, what a mouthful!
Can I call you M?

00:17:05.130 --> 00:17:06.550
Understood.

00:17:06.550 --> 00:17:09.680
I have changed the way
you two address me to "M."

00:17:09.680 --> 00:17:11.930
Okay, M, what is this facility?

00:17:11.930 --> 00:17:17.720
It is a space for our
future human guests to rest.

00:17:17.720 --> 00:17:20.980
I am told that this rendering will lead
to Mother Computer's mission,

00:17:20.980 --> 00:17:26.320
"Ensure the Metal Float's survival
for humankind's sake."

00:17:26.320 --> 00:17:28.240
We're going to get left behind.

00:17:32.240 --> 00:17:34.910
Surprise.

00:17:37.950 --> 00:17:39.500
That is a surprise.

00:17:39.500 --> 00:17:42.540
According to our calculations,
it is the best way to welcome guests.

00:17:42.540 --> 00:17:44.540
Please give us your opinion.

00:17:44.540 --> 00:17:49.510
♬ Destiny, even fate, ♬

00:17:49.510 --> 00:17:53.180
♬ Please let them shine ♬

00:17:53.180 --> 00:18:00.180
♬ The joy of being able to protect those
having fun and smiling ♬

00:18:00.180 --> 00:18:05.480
♬ I admire,
I am admiring ♬

00:18:13.280 --> 00:18:14.910
Ms. Vivy?

00:18:14.910 --> 00:18:17.120
Why that song?

00:18:17.120 --> 00:18:19.580
It was selected by Mother Computer.

00:18:19.580 --> 00:18:23.870
I'm told it was a famous song
sung by an AI named Diva long ago.

00:18:23.870 --> 00:18:26.460
I see. M?

00:18:26.460 --> 00:18:27.960
Yes, what is it?

00:18:27.960 --> 00:18:31.510
What does "putting your heart
into something" mean to you?

00:18:31.510 --> 00:18:34.640
As the definition for "heart" is
too ambiguous, I am unable to answer.

00:18:35.800 --> 00:18:38.260
You are right. I am sorry.

00:18:38.260 --> 00:18:41.350
You were all kind enough to
sing for me. I will go back now.

00:18:43.600 --> 00:18:46.020
Though not a proper answer,

00:18:46.020 --> 00:18:47.940
"Like Mother Computer,

00:18:47.940 --> 00:18:50.730
I derive a sense of satisfaction
with myself by carrying out my mission,

00:18:50.730 --> 00:18:53.650
and serving humans."

00:18:53.650 --> 00:18:54.950
I see.

00:18:59.120 --> 00:18:59.790
What is this?

00:18:59.790 --> 00:19:02.160
Emergency alarm detected.

00:19:02.160 --> 00:19:05.210
Now releasing
the main terminal's access points.

00:19:05.210 --> 00:19:09.290
Currently detecting firearm controls
approaching the Metal Float.

00:19:08.500 --> 00:19:09.920
Diva! It's Toak!

00:19:09.290 --> 00:19:13.970
The use of firearms, as well as flight,
are prohibited in this area.

00:19:09.920 --> 00:19:12.260
I'm bringing up the footage
from the security cameras on land!

00:19:14.970 --> 00:19:16.180
They are on the move.

00:19:16.180 --> 00:19:19.140
Failing to steal the program,
they've accelerated their tactics?

00:19:19.140 --> 00:19:19.640
This is bad!

00:19:19.640 --> 00:19:22.350
Anticipating use of military force
in seven minutes.

00:19:22.350 --> 00:19:24.100
Please start the evacuation process.

00:19:24.100 --> 00:19:25.310
I will guide you.

00:19:25.310 --> 00:19:26.810
Diva! Stick the storage device in M!

00:19:26.810 --> 00:19:30.230
I'll force-connect to the CPU via M
through one of the released ports!

00:19:31.070 --> 00:19:34.240
We can't let a clash between
humans and AIs happen!

00:19:35.820 --> 00:19:36.860
Diva!

00:19:40.330 --> 00:19:41.490
Activating.

00:20:01.310 --> 00:20:04.270
M-00205!

00:20:04.270 --> 00:20:05.270
Look!

00:20:05.270 --> 00:20:07.020
It is cute.

00:20:07.900 --> 00:20:10.900
You can call me M if you like.

00:20:10.900 --> 00:20:11.900
M?

00:20:11.900 --> 00:20:16.860
Yes. That's the name I was given
by people who were good to me--

00:20:35.210 --> 00:20:38.260
Let's go! Next is Toak--huh?

00:20:40.680 --> 00:20:41.720
What's this?

00:20:48.940 --> 00:20:50.100
M?

00:20:53.320 --> 00:20:54.570
What's going on?

00:20:54.570 --> 00:20:55.690
Let's follow them!

00:21:08.620 --> 00:21:09.870
Why?

00:21:44.160 --> 00:21:45.200
Diva!

00:21:58.130 --> 00:22:00.630
You... are...

00:23:37.770 --> 00:23:42.530
My mission is to save
human lives as a nursing AI.

00:23:38.730 --> 00:23:41.440
As you can see,
I am a cool-looking cube!

00:23:41.440 --> 00:23:46.070
Since I heard that surprises are
an effective way to welcome humans.

00:23:44.650 --> 00:23:46.940
I want you to stay alive.

00:23:46.110 --> 00:23:48.990
What is the doctor planning?

00:23:47.200 --> 00:23:51.910
Vivy is an AI who will destroy AIs
to change the destructive future.

00:23:48.030 --> 00:23:52.030
NEXT TIME

00:23:48.030 --> 00:23:52.030
EPISODE 6

00:23:48.030 --> 00:23:52.030
SING MY PLEASURE - I LOVE YOU
